// SHA-256 and HMAC-SHA256 in pure MoonBit, because neither exists in
// moonbitlang/core and Slack's request signature needs both. An FFI binding
// would have made this package native-only, which would in turn have pushed
// signature verification out of reach of a wasm-hosted Slack app.
//
// Bytes in, bytes out, no imports: text encoding is the caller's problem
// (@signature does it with moonbitlang/core/encoding/utf8), which keeps this
// package a straight port of RFC 6234 and RFC 4231 with their vectors as tests.
import {
}

// The RFC vectors are given as ASCII strings and as byte counts; utf8 is how
// the tests turn the former into the latter without assuming MoonBit's UTF-16
// string representation.
import {
  "moonbitlang/core/encoding/utf8",
} for "test"
